ha-citrine source patch 0005 against CitrineOS v2.1.0
(4fd7599b91c2fb6e6065e7c9b94be69880cced27), applied after 0001 to 0004:
OCPP 2.1 message routes validate against their own schema definitions.

With swagger exposeMessage (the App's setting), each message route's body
schema is registered as a shared Fastify schema with a version prefix
("ocpp2.1-SetChargingProfileRequest"), but its definitions are registered under
their bare names ("ChargingProfileType", "ChargingProfilePurposeEnumType").
OCPP 2.0.1 and 2.1 use the same definition names and 2.0.1 is registered
first, so an already-present name is kept and every OCPP 2.1 route validated
its nested objects against the 2.0.1 definitions. A 2.1 SetChargingProfile
with chargingProfilePurpose LocalGeneration or PriorityCharging was refused
with 400 FST_ERR_VALIDATION ("must be equal to one of the allowed values"),
as Trialog's TRIALOG-201 was at the Plugfest (ha-addons#95). 2.1-only fields
were not checked at all.

The patch registers definitions with the same version prefix as the body
schema and points the body's $refs at the prefixed names, so each version's
route resolves its own definitions. Routes registered without a prefix
(querystring and response schemas) are unchanged. A test registers the 2.0.1
and 2.1 SetChargingProfileRequest in that order and checks that LocalGeneration
is accepted on 2.1 only; it fails without the patch.

diff --git a/packages/base/src/util/endpoints/route-schemas.ts b/packages/base/src/util/endpoints/route-schemas.ts
index 1ebdbdf4e..de0873314 100644
--- a/packages/base/src/util/endpoints/route-schemas.ts
+++ b/packages/base/src/util/endpoints/route-schemas.ts
@@ -73,17 +73,22 @@ export function registerRouteSchema(
         if (!definition['$id']) {
           definition['$id'] = key;
         }
-        registerRouteSchema(targets, definition);
+        // ha-citrine patch (0005-ocpp2-route-schema-definitions): definitions get the
+        // version prefix too. OCPP 2.0.1 and 2.1 share definition names
+        // (ChargingProfileType, ChargingProfilePurposeEnumType, ...), so unprefixed the
+        // first version registered served every version's route.
+        registerRouteSchema(targets, definition, schemaIdPrefix);
       });
     }
     if (schemaCopy.properties) {
+      const refPrefix = schemaIdPrefix ?? '';
       Object.keys(schemaCopy.properties).forEach((key) => {
         const property = schemaCopy.properties[key];
         if (property.$ref) {
-          property.$ref = property.$ref.replace('#/definitions/', '');
+          property.$ref = refPrefix + property.$ref.replace('#/definitions/', '');
         }
         if (property.items && property.items.$ref) {
-          property.items.$ref = property.items.$ref.replace('#/definitions/', '');
+          property.items.$ref = refPrefix + property.items.$ref.replace('#/definitions/', '');
         }
       });
     }
diff --git a/packages/base/test/util/endpoints/route-schemas.test.ts b/packages/base/test/util/endpoints/route-schemas.test.ts
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..bd16a5b37
--- /dev/null
